1
00:00:07,170 --> 00:00:09,970
A raffle has tickets numbered 1 to 30.

2
00:00:10,020 --> 00:00:11,470
One ticket is drawn.

3
00:00:11,520 --> 00:00:17,280
You win a prize if the number is a multiple of 7, or a multiple of 11.

4
00:00:17,330 --> 00:00:21,670
Can a number from 1 to 30 be a multiple of both 7 and 11?

5
00:00:21,720 --> 00:00:26,080
Pause the video and choose: no, or yes.

6
00:00:26,130 --> 00:00:26,290
No.

7
00:00:26,340 --> 00:00:31,650
The first number that is a multiple of both is 77, which is too big.

8
00:00:31,700 --> 00:00:40,160
Remember: the probability of an event is the number of favourable outcomes, divided by the total number of outcomes.

9
00:00:40,210 --> 00:00:46,110
Events are mutually exclusive if they cannot happen at the same time.

10
00:00:46,160 --> 00:00:49,990
Multiples of 7 up to 30 are 7, 14, 21 and 28.

11
00:00:50,040 --> 00:00:52,570
Multiples of 11 are 11 and 22.

12
00:00:52,620 --> 00:00:54,500
None is in both.

13
00:00:54,550 --> 00:01:02,390
For mutually exclusive events, the probability of A or B is the probability of A plus the probability of B.

14
00:01:02,440 --> 00:01:03,080
Your turn.

15
00:01:03,130 --> 00:01:06,230
What is the probability of winning the raffle?

16
00:01:06,280 --> 00:01:09,800
Give your answer as a fraction in its simplest form.

17
00:01:09,850 --> 00:01:13,050
Pause the video and try it.

18
00:01:13,100 --> 00:01:18,610
4 thirtieths plus 2 thirtieths is 6 thirtieths, which is a fifth.

19
00:01:18,660 --> 00:01:24,300
Multiples of 3 and even numbers are not mutually exclusive: 6 and 12 are both.

20
00:01:24,350 --> 00:01:27,040
Adding would count them twice.

21
00:01:27,090 --> 00:01:32,820
If mutually exclusive events cover every outcome, their probabilities add up to 1.

22
00:01:32,870 --> 00:01:34,640
Here is a spinner.

23
00:01:34,690 --> 00:01:35,340
Your turn.

24
00:01:35,390 --> 00:01:37,720
What is the probability of yellow?

25
00:01:37,770 --> 00:01:40,660
Pause and work it out.

26
00:01:40,710 --> 00:01:42,980
The others add up to 0.7.

27
00:01:43,030 --> 00:01:45,300
1 minus 0.7 is 0.3.

28
00:01:45,350 --> 00:01:46,670
Here is the method.

29
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:50,270
Step 1: check they cannot happen together.

30
00:01:50,320 --> 00:01:53,770
Step 2: if not, add their probabilities.

31
00:01:53,820 --> 00:01:58,710
Step 3: if they overlap, list and count the outcomes instead.

32
00:01:58,760 --> 00:02:02,430
Step 4: all outcomes together add up to 1.

33
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:04,710
On a dice: less than 3, or a 6.

34
00:02:04,760 --> 00:02:08,700
That is 2 sixths plus 1 sixth, which is a half.

35
00:02:08,750 --> 00:02:14,540
A spinner: P of A is 0.42, P of B is 0.18, P of C is X, and P of D is 2 X.

36
00:02:14,590 --> 00:02:18,010
3 X equals 0.4, so X is 2 fifteenths.

37
00:02:18,060 --> 00:02:21,560
The probability of winning a game is 0.15.

38
00:02:21,610 --> 00:02:25,410
In 200 games, you expect about 30 wins.

39
00:02:25,460 --> 00:02:30,000
On a dice, Ahmed finds the probability of even, or greater than 3.

40
00:02:30,050 --> 00:02:31,950
Which line is wrong?

41
00:02:32,000 --> 00:02:33,160
Line 1 is wrong.

42
00:02:33,210 --> 00:02:36,970
4 and 6 are in both, so the events overlap.

43
00:02:37,020 --> 00:02:39,490
The outcomes are 2, 4, 5 and 6.

44
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:42,490
That is 4 sixths, or 2 thirds.

45
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:50,510
Game designers add the probabilities of separate rewards, to make sure all the chances add up to exactly 1.

46
00:02:50,560 --> 00:02:51,760
One last question.

47
00:02:51,810 --> 00:02:56,920
On a dice, are even and odd mutually exclusive, or not mutually exclusive?

48
00:02:56,970 --> 00:03:00,200
Pause the video and choose.

49
00:03:00,250 --> 00:03:01,540
Mutually exclusive.

50
00:03:01,590 --> 00:03:04,270
No number is both even and odd.

51
00:03:04,320 --> 00:03:08,900
To remember: mutually exclusive events cannot both happen.

52
00:03:08,950 --> 00:03:11,770
Then P of A or B is P of A plus P of B.

53
00:03:11,820 --> 00:03:14,430
All the outcomes add up to 1.

54
00:03:14,480 --> 00:03:17,870
If events overlap, count instead of adding.

55
00:03:17,920 --> 00:03:23,310
Great work! Now practise lesson 12.1 on Camday.
